, where | represents the cursor & مرحبا represents “hello” in Arabic, the ambiguity arises because:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If the cursor is associated with the end of the English word, it would be as if you’re continuing to type in English (LTR).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If the cursor is associated with the beginning of the Arabic word, it would also be as if you’re continuing to type in Arabic (RTL).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/TextSelectionAffinity","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" helps resolve this ambiguity by determining the direction or association of the cursor relative to the surrounding text."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can configure the selection affinity on a given hierarchy by using the "},{"code":"textSelectionAffinity(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier:"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/textselectionaffinity"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TextSelectionAffinity"}],"modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"title":"TextSelectionAffinity","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Enumeration","symbolKind":"enum","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TextSelectionAffinity","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI21TextSelectionAffinityO"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A representation of the direction or association of a selection or cursor relative to a text character."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"This concept becomes much more prominent when dealing w